            {{> components/use-case-link href="/features.html#section-attachments" title="Attachments and inline images" description="Files, streams, and embedded content" core=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/rfc-compliant.html#section-why" title="Why MIME structure matters" description="Correct nesting across mail clients" core=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/configuration.html#section-programmatic-api-common" title="Configure SMTP once" description="Server, credentials, and transport" core=true}}
          </nav>
        </article>

        <article id="secure-sending" class="use-case">
          <div class="use-case-copy">
            <p class="use-case-coordinate">02 · Security</p>
            <h2>Send securely.</h2>
            <p>Protect the SMTP connection with TLS, use a password or refresh-aware OAuth2 token, sign the sending domain with DKIM, or protect message content with S/MIME or OpenPGP/MIME. These are separate layers, so you can apply the ones your mail flow needs.</p>
          </div>
          <nav class="use-case-links" aria-label="Secure sending documentation">
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/security.html#section-authentication-methods" title="TLS and OAuth2" description="Transport and authentication" core=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/security.html#section-sending-dkim" title="DKIM signing" description="Domain identity and integrity" dkim=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/security.html#section-sending-smime" title="S/MIME" description="Sign and encrypt message content" smime=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/security.html#section-sending-openpgp" title="OpenPGP/MIME" description="Sign and encrypt with OpenPGP keys" openpgp=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/security.html#section-crlf-scanning" title="Input scanning" description="Catch suspicious header content" core=true}}
          </nav>
        </article>

        <article id="high-throughput" class="use-case">
          <div class="use-case-copy">
            <p class="use-case-coordinate">03 · Sustained load</p>
            <h2>Handle high throughput.</h2>
            <p>When several workers send continuously, use bounded worker threads and reuse physical SMTP connections in a pool. Cluster keys can keep workloads separate or spread one workload over several SMTP servers.</p>
          </div>
          <nav class="use-case-links" aria-label="High-throughput documentation">
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/features.html#section-sending-asynchronously" title="Asynchronous sending" description="Schedule work and handle results" batch=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/smtp-connection-pooling.html" title="Pool orchestration" description="Choose the API and lifecycle owner" batch=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/configuration.html#section-clustering" title="SMTP clusters" description="Separate and balance workloads" batch=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/configuration.html#section-mailer-lifecycle" title="Mailer lifecycle" description="Finish work and release resources" batch=true}}
          </nav>
        </article>

        <article id="batch-delivery" class="use-case">
          <div class="use-case-copy">
            <p class="use-case-coordinate">04 · Known workloads</p>
            <h2>Send a batch without reconnecting.</h2>
            <p>For a known list or a caller-owned queue, keep one SMTP connection open and send sequentially. This is part of the core API. Move to pooled delivery only when you need concurrency or sustained throughput.</p>
          </div>
          <nav class="use-case-links" aria-label="Batch delivery documentation">
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/features.html#section-sending-asynchronously" title="Simple batches" description="One connection for a known list" core=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/features.html#section-sending-asynchronously" title="Scoped open connection" description="Drive a caller-owned queue" core=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/features.html#section-handling-async-result" title="Asynchronous results" description="Observe success and failure" core=true}}
            {{> components/use-case-link href="/features.html#section-submission-receipts" title="SMTP submission receipts" description="Read the server's replies" core=true}}
          </nav>
        </article>

